</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Conclusion</h3>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We proposed RLHF-COV and DPO-COV algorithms that simultaneously mitigate the <span id="S6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">C<span id="S6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">orruption</span></span>, <span id="S6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">O<span id="S6.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">veroptimization</span></span> and <span id="S6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">V<span id="S6.p1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">erbosity</span></span> issues, in both offline and online settings. This ability is theoretically proved by length-regularized generalization analysis on corrupted data, and empirically demonstrated.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Limitations:</span> This work focuses on simple question and answer, and in the future could be extended to dialogue, reasoning and multimodality, etc. Also, our algorithms cannot totally remove hallucinations that may yield false or unsafe information disclosure, which could be tackled in the future.</p>
</div>
</section>
