<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To further evaluate our algorithm’s robustness to data corruption, we change the labels of randomly selected 25% samples from the Argilla data and implement these algorithms. Similar to Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we summarize the results and hyperparameters on this corrupted data in Table <a href="#A1.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, which shows that both our DPO-COV and the robust DPO are more robust to the corruption than the other non-robust DPO variants, and the outputs of these models again have comparable lengths on the corrupted data.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Experiment on Math and Reasoning</h4>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also compare our Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> with other offline DPO variants over datasets of math and reasoning tasks, including Grade School Math 8K (GSM8K) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite>, AI2 Reasoning Challenge (ARC) tasks (both easy and challenge sets) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Clark et al.,, 2018</a>)</cite>, GPQA (both main and diamond sets) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rein et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>. We run the benchmark test with <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2024a, </a>)</cite> and report the accuracies in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. The model hyper-parameters are the same as in Table <a href="#A1.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. The results shown in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> indicate that our DPO-COV algorithm outperforms the other variants also on most of the math and reasoning tasks.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Experiment on Online Data</h4>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to the offline experiments in Section <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we compare important special cases of Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4 Our Online DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, including our online DPO-COV with all 3 components activated, the online variant of the robust DPO algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bukharin et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>, online optimistic DPO algorithm (named XPO in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>), online length regularized DPO algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024a, </a>)</cite> and online vanilla DPO algorithm (using DPO objective in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Guo et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>). We use zephyr-7b-gemma-sft-v0.1 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">HuggingFaceH4,, 2024</a>)</cite> as the reference model <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> and the initial model <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each algorithm is trained with <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.05</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=3</annotation></semantics></math> iterations. In each iteration, we generate the online labels <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> from pair-preference-model-LLaMA3-8B <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">RLHFlow,, 2024</a>)</cite>, and combine the online data with 50% of the preference dataset of Argilla-DPO-Mix-7K <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Argill,, 2024</a>)</cite>. Then we apply LoRA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al.,, 2021</a>)</cite> and two epochs of the AdamW optimizer <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov and Hutter,, 2017</a>)</cite> with stepsize <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math> to the objective (<a href="#S4.E25" title="Equation 25In Algorithm 2 ‣ 4 Our Online DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). On AlpacaEval 2.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dubois et al.,, 2024</a>)</cite>, we compare the LC-win rates of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm ref}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm ref}</annotation></semantics></math> and that of the models obtained by the above algorithms against the model GPT-4 Preview (11/06) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">OpenAI,, 2024</a>)</cite>. Again, the results in Table <a href="#A1.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ A.1 Experiments on the Offline Argilla Data ‣ Appendix A Experiments ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> indicate that our online DPO-COV algorithm with all three components activated achieves the highest length-controlled win rates.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Supporting Lemmas</h3>

<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in(0,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in(0,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{1},z_{2}\in[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{1},z_{2}\in[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{|z_{1}-z_{2}|}{3+e^{R}}\leq|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|\leq\frac{1}{4}|z_{1}-z_{2}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{|z_{1}-z_{2}|}{3+e^{R}}\leq|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|\leq\frac{1}{4}|z_{1}-z_{2}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark: </span> Our bound (<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is strictly tighter than <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|z_{1}-z_{2}|}{(1+e^{R})^{2}}\leq|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|\leq|z_{1}-z_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|z_{1}-z_{2}|}{(1+e^{R})^{2}}\leq|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|\leq|z_{1}-z_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math> obtained in Lemma A.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2024c, </a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\min}=\min(z_{1},z_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\min}=\min(z_{1},z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{\max}=\max(z_{1},z_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{\max}=\max(z_{1},z_{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|z_{1}-z_{2}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|z_{1}-z_{2}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=z_{\max}-z_{\min}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=z_{\max}-z_{\min},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\sigma(z_{1})-\sigma(z_{2})|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sigma(z_{\max})-\sigma(z_{\min})=\int_{z_{\min}}^{z_{\max}}\sigma^{\prime}(z)dz." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sigma(z_{\max})-\sigma(z_{\min})=\int_{z_{\min}}^{z_{\max}}\sigma^{\prime}(z)dz.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, it suffices to prove that <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}(v)\in\big[\frac{1}{3+e^{R}},\frac{1}{4}\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}(v)\in\big[\frac{1}{3+e^{R}},\frac{1}{4}\big]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in[z_{\min},z_{\max}]\subset[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in[z_{\min},z_{\max}]\subset[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that for any <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in[z_{\min},z_{\max}]\subset[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in[z_{\min},z_{\max}]\subset[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(v)\in[\sigma(-R),\sigma(R)]=[1-\sigma(R),\sigma(R)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(v)\in[\sigma(-R),\sigma(R)]=[1-\sigma(R),\sigma(R)]</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, we conclude the proof by the following two bounds.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{\prime}(v)=\sigma(v)[1-\sigma(v)]=\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(v)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}\leq\frac{1}{4}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{\prime}(v)=\sigma(v)[1-\sigma(v)]=\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(v)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}\leq\frac{1}{4}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A2.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma^{\prime}(v)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma^{\prime}(v)=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(v)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(v)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(R)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{4}-\Big[\sigma(R)-\frac{1}{2}\Big]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sigma(R)[1-\sigma(R)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sigma(R)[1-\sigma(R)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{1+e^{R}}\frac{e^{R}}{1+e^{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{1+e^{R}}\frac{e^{R}}{1+e^{R}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{(1+e^{R})(1+e^{-R})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{(1+e^{R})(1+e^{-R})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{2+e^{R}+e^{-R}}\geq\frac{1}{3+e^{R}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{2+e^{R}+e^{-R}}\geq\frac{1}{3+e^{R}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0},a_{1}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0},a_{1}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the following equality holds</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})=r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})=r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined by Eqs. (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) respectively. Furthermore, under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, both sides of the above Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) range in <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-R,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-R,R]</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\omega(|a_{1}|-|a_{0}|)+\beta\log\Big(\frac{\pi_{r}(a_{1}|x)\pi_{\rm ref}(a_{0}|x)}{\pi_{r}(a_{0}|x)\pi_{\rm ref}(a_{1}|x)}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\omega(|a_{1}|-|a_{0}|)+\beta\log\Big(\frac{\pi_{r}(a_{1}|x)\pi_{\rm ref}(a_{0}|x)}{\pi_{r}(a_{0}|x)\pi_{\rm ref}(a_{1}|x)}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{=}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and (b) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x,a_{0}),r(x,a_{1})\in[0,R]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x,a_{0}),r(x,a_{1})\in[0,R]</annotation></semantics></math>, so</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})=r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})\in[-R,R]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})=r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})\in[-R,R].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 3</span></span><span id="Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Any policy <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi_{r^{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{r^{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> are defined by Eqs. (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and (<a href="#S3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) respectively. Furthermore, under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, any <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|r^{\pi}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi}(x,a_{0})|\leq R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|r^{\pi}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi}(x,a_{0})|\leq R</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{0},a_{1}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{0},a_{1}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Eq. (<a href="#S3.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) implies that for any <math id="A2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]=\pi(a|x)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]=\pi(a|x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{r^{\pi}}(x)=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(a|x)=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{r^{\pi}}(x)=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]=\sum_{a\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(a|x)=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, <math id="A2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi_{r^{\pi}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{r^{\pi}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be proved as follows.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi_{r^{\pi}}(a|x)\overset{(a)}{=}\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)}{Z_{r^{\pi}}(x)}\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]\overset{(b)}{=}\pi(a|x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi_{r^{\pi}}(a|x)\overset{(a)}{=}\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a|x)}{Z_{r^{\pi}}(x)}\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\pi}(x,a)-\omega|a|}{\beta}\Big]\overset{(b)}{=}\pi(a|x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and (b) uses Eqs. (<a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">When <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|r^{\pi}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi}(x,a_{0})|\overset{(a)}{=}|r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})|\overset{(b)}{=}|r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})|\overset{(c)}{\leq}R," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|r^{\pi}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi}(x,a_{0})|\overset{(a)}{=}|r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{1})-r^{\pi_{r}}(x,a_{0})|\overset{(b)}{=}|r(x,a_{1})-r(x,a_{0})|\overset{(c)}{\leq}R,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses <math id="A2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi=\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi=\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, (b) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) and (c) uses Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4</span></span><span id="Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, for any <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{r,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{r,i}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>), the following inequality holds.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\leq\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]+\sigma(R)|\xi_{r,i}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\leq\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]+\sigma(R)|\xi_{r,i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{\mathcal{R}}\overset{\rm def}{=}\{\pi_{r}:r\in\mathcal{R}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}^{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}^{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>), the following inequality holds.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\sigma[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}]\leq\log\sigma[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]+\sigma(R)|\xi_{i}^{\pi}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\sigma[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}]\leq\log\sigma[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]+\sigma(R)|\xi_{i}^{\pi}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\xi_{r,i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\xi_{r,i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text"> by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) since <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then Eq. (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Lemma 4. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) follows from <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\leq\sigma(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\leq\sigma(R)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p7.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\in[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell}),r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\subseteq[-R,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell}),r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\subseteq[-R,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subset</annotation></semantics></math> is implied by Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, <math id="A2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) since <math id="A2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then Eq. (<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Lemma 4. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) follows from <math id="A2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\leq\sigma(R)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\leq\sigma(R)</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p8.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="v\in[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell}),r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}]\subseteq[-R,+\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mi>π</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mi>R</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in[r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell}),r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\pi}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{\pi}]\subseteq[-R,+\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\subset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊂</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\subset</annotation></semantics></math> is implied by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma3" title="Lemma 3. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 5</span></span><span id="Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and reward models <math id="Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,r^{\prime}:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,r^{\prime}:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{A}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big\{\sigma[r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}]-\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]\big\}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big\{\sigma[r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}]-\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]\big\}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E34.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big\{\sigma[r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]-\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]\big\}^{2}-\frac{1}{2}|\xi_{i}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big\{\sigma[r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]-\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]\big\}^{2}-\frac{1}{2}|\xi_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\prime}=r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\prime}=r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{\prime}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}=r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}=r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the following function.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(u)=\big[\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)-\sigma(A_{i})\big]^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(u)=\big[\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)-\sigma(A_{i})\big]^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Note that the range of the sigmoid function <math id="A2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, for any <math id="A2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{du}f(u)=2\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)\big[1-\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)\big]\big[\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)-\sigma(A_{i})\big]\in\Big(-\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{du}f(u)=2\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)\big[1-\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)\big]\big[\sigma(A_{i}^{\prime}+u)-\sigma(A_{i})\big]\in\Big(-\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(0)-f(y_{i}\xi_{i})\leq|f(y_{i}\xi_{i})-f(0)|\leq\frac{1}{2}|y_{i}\xi_{i}|=\frac{1}{2}|\xi_{i}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(0)-f(y_{i}\xi_{i})\leq|f(y_{i}\xi_{i})-f(0)|\leq\frac{1}{2}|y_{i}\xi_{i}|=\frac{1}{2}|\xi_{i}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">which implies Eq. (<a href="#A2.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 6</span></span><span id="Thmlemma6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, the policies <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{r^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{r^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by the analytical solution (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) satisfy</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|\log\frac{\pi_{r^{\prime}}(a|x)}{\pi_{r}(a|x)}\Big|\leq\frac{2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}}{\beta}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|\log\frac{\pi_{r^{\prime}}(a|x)}{\pi_{r}(a|x)}\Big|\leq\frac{2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}}{\beta},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}=\sup_{x\in\mathcal{X},a\in\mathcal{A}}|r^{\prime}(x,a)-r(x,a)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}=\sup_{x\in\mathcal{X},a\in\mathcal{A}}|r^{\prime}(x,a)-r(x,a)|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Note that for any <math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r,r^{\prime}\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-r(x,a^{\prime})}{\beta}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\Big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-r(x,a^{\prime})}{\beta}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\big[\exp(-\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big[\exp(-\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}{Z_{r}(x)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}{Z_{r}(x)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\sum_{a^{\prime}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\big[\exp(-\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big[\exp(-\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">As a result,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{r^{\prime}}(a|x)}{\pi_{r}(a|x)}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\pi_{r^{\prime}}(a|x)}{\pi_{r}(a|x)}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big(\frac{Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}{Z_{r}(x)}\Big)^{-1}\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big(\frac{Z_{r^{\prime}}(x)}{Z_{r}(x)}\Big)^{-1}\frac{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r^{\prime}(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}{\pi_{\rm ref}(a^{\prime}|x)\exp\big[\frac{r(x,a^{\prime})-\omega|a^{\prime}|}{\beta}\big]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\in" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>∈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\in</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E38.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\big[\exp(-2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big[\exp(-2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta),\exp(2\|r^{\prime}-r\|_{\infty}/\beta)\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">which directly implies Eq. (<a href="#A2.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Lemma 6. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We slightly adjust Theorem 13.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang,, 2023</a>)</cite> as follows, by using filtration <math id="A2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}_{t}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}_{t}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> (so the conditional expectation becomes the total expectation), replacing <math id="A2.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and negating the small probability event.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 7</span></span><span id="Thmlemma7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider random variables <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{Z_{i}\}_{i=0}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{Z_{i}\}_{i=0}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the following inequality holds simultaneously for all <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=1,2,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=1,2,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math> with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}\leq\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\lambda^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{\prime}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\lambda^{\prime}Z_{i})]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i=1}^{n}Z_{i}\leq\frac{\log(1/\delta)}{\lambda^{\prime}}+\frac{1}{\lambda^{\prime}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\lambda^{\prime}Z_{i})].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 8</span></span><span id="Thmlemma8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in[\sigma(R),1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in[\sigma(R),1]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>. Under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 3.1 Our Offline RLHF-COV Objective ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, the following bound holds for any <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{r}=[\xi_{r,1},\ldots,\xi_{r,N}]\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{r}=[\xi_{r,1},\ldots,\xi_{r,N}]\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> (given by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>)) simultaneously with probability at least <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})\leq\frac{2}{N}\Big[\|\xi^{*}\|_{1}+\log\Big(\frac{|\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})|}{\delta}\Big)\Big]-\frac{E_{r}^{2}}{2(3+e^{R})^{2}}+7\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})\leq\frac{2}{N}\Big[\|\xi^{*}\|_{1}+\log\Big(\frac{|\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})|}{\delta}\Big)\Big]-\frac{E_{r}^{2}}{2(3+e^{R})^{2}}+7\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{r}:=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\big|r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})-r(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})+r(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})\big|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{r}:=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\big|r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})-r(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})+r(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})\big|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>-cover of <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, that is, for any <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{{\dagger}}\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{{\dagger}}\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="Thmlemma8.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.8" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">Based on Assumption <a href="#Thmassum1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 3.1 Our Offline RLHF-COV Objective ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, given <math id="A2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})</annotation></semantics></math>, the target label <math id="A2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\{-1,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\{-1,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> as well as the underlying reward <math id="A2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and noise <math id="A2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the event <math id="A2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}=y</annotation></semantics></math> occurs with the following probability.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{r,\xi_{i}}(y|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{r,\xi_{i}}(y|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{cases}\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(-1)})+\xi_{i}],&amp;y=1\\
\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(-1)})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)})-\xi_{i}],&amp;y=-1.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{cases}\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(-1)})+\xi_{i}],&amp;y=1\\
\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(-1)})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)})-\xi_{i}],&amp;y=-1.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.2.1" class="ltx_text">By merging the two cases above, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{r,\xi_{i}}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})=\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{r,\xi_{i}}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})=\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.3.1" class="ltx_text">Define the following random variables for <math id="A2.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,\ldots,N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,\ldots,N</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z_{i}(r)=\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]}{\sigma[r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{*}]}=\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{p_{r,0}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})}{p_{r^{*},\xi_{i}^{*}}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z_{i}(r)=\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})]}{\sigma[r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+y_{i}\xi_{i}^{*}]}=\frac{1}{2}\log\frac{p_{r,0}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})}{p_{r^{*},\xi_{i}^{*}}(y_{i}|x_{i},a_{i}^{(1)},a_{i}^{(-1)})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.4.1" class="ltx_text">Then the following inequality holds for finitely many <math id="A2.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously with probability at least <math id="A2.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\!\sum_{i=1}^{N}\!\big\{\!\log\!\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!+\!y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\!-\!\log\!\sigma[r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!+\!y_{i}\xi_{i}^{*}]\!+\!\lambda(|\xi_{i}^{*}|\!-\!|\xi_{r,i}|)\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\!\sum_{i=1}^{N}\!\big\{\!\log\!\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!+\!y_{i}\xi_{r,i}]\!-\!\log\!\sigma[r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r^{*}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!+\!y_{i}\xi_{i}^{*}]\!+\!\lambda(|\xi_{i}^{*}|\!-\!|\xi_{r,i}|)\big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
