<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{N}\Big[\|\xi^{*}\|_{1}+\log\Big(\frac{|\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})|}{\delta}\Big)\Big]-\frac{E_{r}^{2}}{2(3+e^{R})^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>δ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{N}\Big[\|\xi^{*}\|_{1}+\log\Big(\frac{|\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})|}{\delta}\Big)\Big]-\frac{E_{r}^{2}}{2(3+e^{R})^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p12.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p12.5.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Lemma 4. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma4" title="Lemma 4. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, (b) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) and <math id="A2.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(R)\leq\lambda\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(R)\leq\lambda\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, (c) denotes <math id="A2.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math> as the expectation under Assumption <a href="#Thmassum1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 3.1 Our Offline RLHF-COV Objective ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and (c) holds for finitely many <math id="A2.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously with probability at least <math id="A2.p12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> (by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> with <math id="A2.p12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda^{\prime}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda^{\prime}=1</annotation></semantics></math>), (d) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) and Assumption <a href="#Thmassum1" title="Assumption 1. ‣ 3.1 Our Offline RLHF-COV Objective ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, (e) uses <math id="A2.p12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log v\leq v-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log v\leq v-1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p12.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, (f) uses Lemma 12.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harsha,, 2011</a>)</cite>, (g) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), (h) uses Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, (i) uses Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> as well as the fact that the <math id="A2.p12.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> samples <math id="A2.p12.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i},a_{i}^{w},a_{i}^{\ell}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i},a_{i}^{w},a_{i}^{\ell}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d., (j) denotes <math id="A2.p12.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{r}:=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\big|r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})-r(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})+r(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})\big|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{r}:=\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathcal{D}}\big|r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})-r^{*}(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})-r(x_{1},a_{1}^{w})+r(x_{1},a_{1}^{\ell})\big|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have proved that with probability at least <math id="A2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the event <math id="A2.p13.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}:=\{" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mo stretchy="false">{</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}:=\{</annotation></semantics></math>Eq. (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) holds for all <math id="A2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously<math id="A2.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">}</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\}</annotation></semantics></math> occurs. We will extend the range to any <math id="A2.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>. By the definition of the <math id="A2.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> cover <math id="A2.p13.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists at least one <math id="A2.p13.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{{\dagger}}\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{{\dagger}}\in\mathcal{N}_{\epsilon}(\mathcal{R})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.p13.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\big|\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\big|\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">a</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(a)}{=}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex52.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big\{\!\log\sigma[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}]-\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r,i}]\big\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\big\{\!\log\sigma[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}]-\log\sigma[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r,i}]\big\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\lambda}{N}(\|\xi_{r}\|_{1}-\|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}}\|_{1})\Big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\lambda}{N}(\|\xi_{r}\|_{1}-\|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}}\|_{1})\Big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">b</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(b)}{\leq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex54.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}]-[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r,i}]\big|+\lambda(|\xi_{r,i}|-|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}|)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}]-[r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})+\xi_{r,i}]\big|+\lambda(|\xi_{r,i}|-|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}|)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex55.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\big|+\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|+\big|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}-\xi_{r,i}\big|+\lambda(|\xi_{r,i}-\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}|)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\big|+\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|+\big|\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}-\xi_{r,i}\big|+\lambda(|\xi_{r,i}-\xi_{r^{{\dagger}},i}|)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{\leq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">c</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(c)}{\leq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex56.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\big|+\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\Big[\big|r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\big|+\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+(\lambda+1)\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})]\big|\Big]\overset{(d)}{\leq}6\epsilon," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">d</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><mn>6</mn><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+(\lambda+1)\big|r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})-[r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r^{{\dagger}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})]\big|\Big]\overset{(d)}{\leq}6\epsilon,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses the definition of <math id="A2.p13.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> given by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="Equation 8 ‣ 3.1 Our Offline RLHF-COV Objective ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>), (b) uses triangle inequality and <math id="A2.p13.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dv}[\log\sigma(v)]=\sigma(-v)\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p13.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, (c) uses the property that <math id="A2.p13.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{r,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{r,i}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by Eq. (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Proposition 1. ‣ 3.2 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) is a 1-Lipschitz continuous function of <math id="A2.p13.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})-r(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})</annotation></semantics></math> (since <math id="A2.p13.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max(\cdot,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max(\cdot,0)</annotation></semantics></math> is 1-Lipschitz continuous), (d) uses <math id="A2.p13.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r^{{\dagger}}-r\|_{\infty}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p13.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Under the event <math id="A2.p13.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, Eq. (<a href="#A2.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) holds with <math id="A2.p13.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A2.p13.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, which along with Eq. (<a href="#A2.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) implies the following inequality.</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex58.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle[\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})]+[\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle[\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r,\xi_{r})]+[\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{*},\xi^{*})-\mathcal{L}_{N,\lambda}(r^{{\dagger}},\xi_{r^{{\dagger}}})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
