<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\overset{(e)}{\leq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.700em">e</mi><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em">)</mo></mrow></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\overset{(e)}{\leq}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Big\{|\xi_{i}^{*}|\!-\!\frac{2}{(3+e^{R})^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mu_{i}}\Big[\big|r^{\pi_{r^{*}}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r^{\pi_{r^{*}}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!-\!r^{\pi^{\prime}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!+\!r^{\pi^{\prime}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|^{2}\Big]\Big\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>R</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{8}\sum_{i=1}^{t}\Big\{|\xi_{i}^{*}|\!-\!\frac{2}{(3+e^{R})^{2}}\mathbb{E}_{\mu_{i}}\Big[\big|r^{\pi_{r^{*}}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!-\!r^{\pi_{r^{*}}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\!-\!r^{\pi^{\prime}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{w})\!+\!r^{\pi^{\prime}}(x_{i},a_{i}^{\ell})\big|^{2}\Big]\Big\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p16.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p16.5.1" class="ltx_text">where (a) uses <math id="A2.p16.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log v\leq v-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log v\leq v-1</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A2.p16.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, (b) uses Lemma 12.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Harsha,, 2011</a>)</cite>, (c) uses Eqs. (<a href="#A2.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>), (d) uses Eq. (<a href="#A2.E29" title="Equation 29 ‣ Lemma 2. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>) and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and (e) uses Assumption <a href="#Thmassum2" title="Assumption 2 (Realizable and Bounded Reward ( , )). ‣ 3.3 Generalization Analysis of Offline DPO-COV ‣ 3 Our Offline DPO-COV Algorithm ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Combining Eqs. (<a href="#A2.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) and (<a href="#A2.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Proof. ‣ Appendix B Supporting Lemmas ‣ Appendix ‣ Provably Mitigating Corruption, Overoptimization, and Verbosity Simultaneously in Offline and Online RLHF/DPO Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), we obtain the following inequality which holds for all <math id="A2.p16.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1,\ldots,T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1,\ldots,T</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p16.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> simultaneously with probability at least <math id="A2.p16.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
